{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason requires calculating the mean of all outcomes for each lottery, treating each outcome as equally weighted regardless of its probability. For Lottery A, the outcomes are 6000 and 0 (two distinct outcomes), so the mean is (6000 + 0) / 2 = 3000. For Lottery B, the outcomes are 4000, 2000, and 0 (three distinct outcomes), so the mean is (4000 + 2000 + 0) / 3 = 2000. According to the decision reason, Lottery A would be preferred because its outcome mean (3000) is higher than that of Lottery B (2000).",
